    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nwhen pasting long line of text from global clipboard using cmd-v (in mac), the text line are all scrambled up.\r\n\r\nProbably due to the cursor going all over the place while pasting in mac is 1 line at a time.\r\n\r\ndoes not happen if pasting done through \"+p\r\n\r\nany way to fix this?\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. open empty buffer\r\n2. copy long text (100-200 lines)\r\n3. paste using cmd-v\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\ntext pasted in order\n\n### Actual behavior\n\ntext scrambled",
